If `dotnet ef` is not available, install it first:
```bash
dotnet tool install --global dotnet-ef
```

Then update the database:
```bash
dotnet ef database update
```

### 12. Build verification

Run `dotnet build` from the solution root to ensure everything compiles.

IMPORTANT: The server project needs a project reference to the Client project to use `IShipmentService` and `Shipment` model. Check that the server `.csproj` already has `<ProjectReference Include="..\ShipmentTracker.Client\ShipmentTracker.Client.csproj" />`. It should since it was scaffolded with Auto mode.

Also make sure to add `Microsoft.Extensions.Http` package to the Client project for `AddHttpClient`:
```bash
cd /tmp/sv-2ef9775457ca4a7f855a10bb985ebc1b/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Client
dotnet add package Microsoft.Extensions.Http
